I walk upstairs to the exhibition.
There are many old pictures here.
I stop in front of a very large black-and-white photograph.
This picture is incredibly fascinating.
It shows a busy harbor with large factories.
I can also see many tall chimneys and dark ships.
These ships look very heavy.
I read the small text next to the photograph.
The text explains the history of this harbor.
A hundred years ago, the area was an industrial zone.
It was a loud and dirty place back then.
The contrast to today is enormous.
Now, this waterfront is quiet and clean.
I often go for a walk along the water on the weekends.
It is hard to imagine the old factories here.
I look at this photograph for a long time.
Then I slowly walk on into the next room.
